  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">English &amp; School Education: English Connects</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As a wholly digital offer open to all teachers and teacher educators, English Connects has ODA benefits. These are predominantly in the area of improved English language teaching and resultant improved English language learning. English Connects will support the UK government&#x2019;s commitment to international development, featuring Sustainable Development Goals around quality education, gender equality, inclusion, human rights and climate change.Foreign language proficiency, English proficiency in particular, has important positive impacts for individual teachers and learners, in particular wider access to employability alongside other economic and social benefits.More widely, our support for individual teacher development provides opportunities for growth, human capital accumulation, leading to development and prosperity more widely.Why we do it:&#x25fc; 1. Equitable improvements in English language teaching through improved knowledge, skills and motivation to contribute to inclusive, quality teaching, learning and assessment of English.&#x25fc; 2. Improved and more equitable English language teacher education and support to teachers.&#x25fc; 3. Individual practitioners are recognised as experts in their context and have more agency to influence wider change in English language teaching and learning.&#x25fc; 4. Fewer inequalities and improved employability and career pathways.&#x25fc; 5. Positioning the UK as an exemplar of high-quality technology-enabled professional development.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">English Connects is one of the Global Programmes through which the British Council delivers its grant-funded activity. The primary focus of this Global Programme is ODA eligible activity and outcomes.English Connects provides professional development opportunities for a global community of English language teaching professionals and practitioners to contribute to education systems that support inclusive, quality teaching, learning and assessment of English to ultimately improve English language skills around the world. We bring together teachers and teacher educators of English worldwide through a global technology-enabled programme delivered by our TeachingEnglish platforms and collaborators. English Connects provides professional development opportunities, practical resources, peer support, professional agency with a range of perspectives and UK expertise to an online community of English language teaching practitioners globally. It helps them to take charge of their own learning, build professional networks and grow their careers. It also provides a unique evidence base to understand challenges and trends in English language teaching worldwide.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The target audiences for this programme are: &#x25fc; Teachers &#x25fc; Teacher educators&#x25fc; Researchers&#x25fc; School leaders&#x25fc; Teaching Associations</narrative>
  </description>
